            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78662",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78662"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-78662?s=golang&n=crypto&ns=golang.org%2Fx&t=golang&vr=%3C0.56.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Previously, a channel registered in the mux's chanList is not usable until it is established. A malicious peer was able flood the channel's incomingRequests, deadlocking the entire connection.\n\nNow, we add an atomic established state, set when a channel becomes usable. Until such a time, handlePacket drops every packet other than the open confirmation/failure, without blocking and without tearing down the connection.\n",
                "markdown": "> Previously, a channel registered in the mux's chanList is not usable until it is established. A malicious peer was able flood the channel's incomingRequests, deadlocking the entire connection.\n\nNow, we add an atomic established state, set when a channel becomes usable. Until such a time, handlePacket drops every packet other than the open confirmation/failure, without blocking and without tearing down the connection.\n\n|                                                       |\n|Package         pkg:golang/golang.org/x/crypto@0.55.0  |\n|Affected range  <0.56.0                                |\n|Fixed version   0.56.0                                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<0.56.0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "0.56.0",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/crypto@0.55.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
